## Assignment Implementation Overview

This assignment was completed by creating a graph database benchmarking environment to compare the performance of multiple graph database platforms.

First, a public graph dataset (cit-HepPh citation network) was selected and prepared. The dataset was then loaded into four different graph databases: Neo4j, Memgraph, ArangoDB, and CognoDB using custom Python scripts.

After successfully loading the data, benchmark scripts were developed to execute different graph workloads, including point lookups, 1-hop, 2-hop, 3-hop traversals, and aggregation queries. Each query was executed multiple times, and performance metrics such as p50 and p95 latency were calculated.

Finally, the collected results were stored, analyzed, and visualized to compare the performance characteristics of each graph database. The complete implementation, results, and documentation were uploaded to GitHub.
